<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José María Velasco Ibarra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José María Velasco <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibarra">Ibarra</a> was the dominant figure in Ecuadorian politics for four decades, who held the presidency five times between 1934 and 1972 but completed only one full term, from 1952 to 1956. A charismatic populist orator, he was overthrown by the army four times, the last in 1972. His career showed both the appeal of personal leadership and the fragility of Ecuador's institutions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-maria-velasco-ibarra.jpg" alt="José María Velasco Ibarra" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Mar%C3%ADa_Velasco_Ibarra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
